Z||000008||Dan86gt3.8||12-27-2000||11:18 AM||||That close up of the gt window was taken for purpose.  That is one of the guys on the board that sells the gt windows.  It's called the fiero wharehouse.  Thoose windows are great, the best purchase/deal/repair or whatever that I have EVER done (well aside from the engine swap).  As you can tell from the pic they look great and fit great.  <P>And thank you once again 2xsess for doing all the pic posting!  <P>thanks chadman, I love my wheels, I thinkj they look great on the fiero!  They look even better when they are all spit shined up.  I have never seen any other fieros with thoose wheels before so I would like to think I pioneered them.  But I see them on ricers alott so that dis-pleases me, as it would most hard working americans.  My only regret is that I should have held out for some 16's but at the time I was a poor highschool kid and shelling out the extra money for tires sounded ludicrous at the time.  Little did I know that I could have got some futura's (sp?) to tide me over till I could by some real tires!<P>------------------<BR>86 gt fiero<BR>3.8/4speed auto<BR>ace conversion kit<BR>1/4- 15.3@90mph||||reg||1
Z||000009||Dan86gt3.8||12-27-2000||11:24 AM||||I would lower it, but the town my school is in as some crazy killer hills!  I have already messed up my front bumper by grinding the hell out of it going up a hill that I swear (no exageration) was like at least a 50-60 degree incline!<P>As far as a "trunk seal"  I don't know exaclty what you mean but I'll look in to it...||||reg||1
Z||000010||Seanh||12-27-2000||01:21 PM||||By Trunk Seal I meant the rectangle peice of rubber that seals the trunk with the underside of the decklid when closed. It looks like there is not one on there because of the carpet edge, it usally fits under the edge of the seal.||||reg||1
